{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur homeowners face gutter challenges that most cities don't. The Tennessee River wraps around your city, Wheeler Lake sits nearby, and the Wheeler Wildlife Refuge stretches across thousands of acres of wetland just north of town. That's a lot of water — and it affects your home in ways you might not expect.</p>

<p>Decatur's water table sits higher than most of North Alabama. During wet seasons, groundwater levels can rise to just a few feet below your foundation. When your gutters overflow or fail, you're adding roof runoff to soil that's already saturated from below. The result is hydrostatic pressure against your basement walls and moisture creeping into places it shouldn't be.</p>

<p>The city's diverse housing stock makes this even more complex. Historic homes in Albany and downtown were built on higher ground — the original settlers knew what they were doing — but many have original or early-replacement gutters that are undersized for modern rainfall intensity. Meanwhile, newer construction in Southwest Decatur and the Highway 31 corridor often came with builder-grade systems that meet code and nothing more.</p>

<p>Decatur's humidity accelerates the problem. Sectional gutters rely on sealant at every joint. In the muggy air near the river, that sealant breaks down faster. We regularly see 10-year-old sectional gutters in Decatur that are leaking at every seam. Seamless gutters eliminate most of those joints entirely — fewer weak points means longer life in your demanding environment.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together, seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>The difference matters in Decatur. Every seam in a gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time. In your humid river-town climate, seams also corrode faster as sealant breaks down. Seamless gutters eliminate these problems by eliminating the seams themselves.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Decatur home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline — not generic sections forced to fit. For historic homes in Albany, we also offer half-round profiles in copper or painted aluminum that maintain period-appropriate aesthetics while dramatically improving performance.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been serving Morgan County homeowners for over 20 years — long enough to understand what the Tennessee River does to homes and what solutions actually work here. We're not a franchise following a national playbook. We're local professionals who know Decatur's unique challenges intimately.</p>

<p>We understand the difference between installing gutters on a 1925 Albany home and a 2020 Southwest Decatur build. We know which neighborhoods have high water table issues and which ones need extra-capacity downspouts. And we know that Decatur's humidity means recommending products and installation methods that wouldn't be necessary just 20 miles inland.</p>
{% endset %}
